# Backend — NestJS

## Project Facts

- Framework: NestJS 11
- ORM: Prisma (to be added)
- Database: PostgreSQL
- Job queue: BullMQ + Redis (to be added)
- Package manager: pnpm

## Module Structure

Each feature is a NestJS module with controller, service, and repository:

```
src/
├── plans/
│   ├── plans.module.ts
│   ├── plans.controller.ts   ← HTTP handlers only, no logic
│   ├── plans.service.ts      ← business logic
│   └── plans.repository.ts  ← Prisma queries
├── suggestions/
├── positions/
├── agents/
└── common/
    ├── prisma/               ← PrismaService
    └── filters/              ← global exception filter
```

## Controller Rules

- Thin handlers only — parse input, call service, return result
- Use `@HttpCode` explicitly for non-200 responses
- Use class-validator DTOs for all request bodies

## Service Rules

- All business logic lives in the service
- Services call repositories, not Prisma directly
- Throw `NotFoundException`, `BadRequestException` etc. from `@nestjs/common`

## Response Format

Always return consistent JSON:
```typescript
// success
{ data: T }

// error (handled by global filter)
{ error: string, statusCode: number }
```

## Domain Modules to Build

- `plans` — TradingPlan CRUD
- `suggestions` — Suggestion generation (dummy → LLM later)
- `positions` — Position lifecycle, confidence updates
- `trades` — Individual trade records
- `agents` — Discovery + trading agent orchestration
